From 5623c96db17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: write per-tile VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID for A22X
 non-binning path (webOS encoding)

The A22X (Adreno 220 / Leia) tile-rendering path has historically shown
a deterministic period-8 pixel-hash render cycle. Visual analysis
revealed these are GMEM tile-coverage failures (different subsets of
the 2x3 GMEM tile grid get rendered per submit), not "wrong-colour
renders" as previously characterised.

Root cause: Mesa freedreno's fd2_gmem.c:60-64 disables hw_binning for
A22X (marked TODO since forever). The A22X hardware binner is
nevertheless active under the hood; with VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID_MIN=MAX=0
the binner uses internal state to choose tile coverage, producing
2^3 = 8 distinct visibility patterns per submit.

Fix: in fd2_emit_tile_renderprep, when not using hw binning AND on
A22X, write VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID_MIN=MAX per tile using the encoding
observed in the closed-source webOS libGLESv2.so decompilation:

    bin_id = (col + 1) | (row << 3)

The +1 offset is on the column field only (not row, unlike the A20X
reference convention in freedreno_gmem.c:392). For the standard
1024x768 / 2x3 tile layout the per-tile bin_ids are 0x01, 0x02,
0x09, 0x0a, 0x11, 0x12 - all non-zero, all distinct. The (col+1)
ensures the col-zero case lands on 1 instead of 0, the value the
binner cycles around.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c | 48 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
@@ -729,6 +729,54 @@ fd2_emit_tile_renderprep(struct fd_batch *batch,
       /* TODO only emit this when tile->p changes */
       OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS, 1);
       OUT_RELOC(ring, pipe_bo, 0, 0, 0);
+   } else if (is_a22x(ctx->screen)) {
+      /*
+       * A22X period-8 render-cycle fix: explicitly write per-tile bin ID.
+       *
+       * Without hardware binning enabled (use_hw_binning() returns false
+       * for A22X - "TODO" in this file), Mesa previously left
+       * VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID_MIN = MAX = 0 throughout the tile loop (set
+       * once in fd2_emit_tile_init with the comment "for some reason
+       * hardware doesn't like certain values"). The A22X hardware binner
+       * is nevertheless active under the hood; with bin_id pinned at 0
+       * it uses some internal-counter state to decide tile coverage,
+       * producing a deterministic 8-pattern visibility cycle observed
+       * across many investigations.
+       *
+       * Encoding (revised 2026-05-11 from webOS libGLESv2.so decomp):
+       *   bin_id = (col + 1) | (row << 3)
+       *
+       * Initial v1 attempted the A20X reference encoding
+       * (((row+1) << 3) | (col+1) from freedreno_gmem.c:392) which
+       * produced no effect. Deeper analysis of the webOS proprietary
+       * decomp showed the pattern:
+       *   uVar24 = uVar27 + 1 | iVar5 * 8 | uVar24;
+       * which decodes as (col+1) | (row<<3) - col gets the +1
+       * offset, row does not. This produces bin_id=0x01 for the
+       * first tile rather than 0x09.
+       *
+       * For the standard 1024x768 / 2x3 tile layout this produces
+       * bin_ids 0x01, 0x02, 0x09, 0x0a, 0x11, 0x12 - all non-zero,
+       * all distinct. The (col+1) ensures the col-zero case lands
+       * on 1 instead of 0 (the "reserved" value the binner cycles
+       * around).
+       */
+      uint32_t col = tile->xoff / tile->bin_w;
+      uint32_t row = tile->yoff / tile->bin_h;
+      uint32_t bin_id = (col + 1) | (row << 3);
+
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
+      OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID_MIN));
+      OUT_RING(ring, bin_id);
+
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
+      OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID_MAX));
+      OUT_RING(ring, bin_id);
    }
 }
